@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.726 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [407 x i8] }> <{ [407 x i8] c"The title of the outline.\0A\0A- When set to `{auto}`, an appropriate title for the\0A  [text language]($text.lang) will be used. This is the default.\0A- When set to `{none}`, the outline will not have a title.\0A- A custom title can be set by passing content.\0A\0AThe outline's heading will not be numbered by default, but you can\0Aforce it to be with a show-set rule:\0A`{show outline: set heading(numbering: \221.\22)}`\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.727 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [382 x i8] }> <{ [382 x i8] c"The type of element to include in the outline.\0A\0ATo list figures containing a specific kind of element, like a table, you\0Acan write `{figure.where(kind: table)}`.\0A\0A```example\0A#outline(\0A  title: [List of Tables],\0A  target: figure.where(kind: table),\0A)\0A\0A#figure(\0A  table(\0A    columns: 4,\0A    [t], [1], [2], [3],\0A    [y], [0.3], [0.7], [0.5],\0A  ),\0A  caption: [Experiment results],\0A)\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.728 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [263 x i8] }> <{ [263 x i8] c"The maximum level up to which elements are included in the outline. When\0Athis argument is `{none}`, all elements are included.\0A\0A```example\0A#set heading(numbering: \221.\22)\0A#outline(depth: 2)\0A\0A= Yes\0ATop-level section.\0A\0A== Still\0ASubsection.\0A\0A=== Nope\0ANot included.\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.729 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1468 x i8] }> <{ [1468 x i8] c"How to indent the outline's entries.\0A\0A- `{none}`: No indent\0A- `{auto}`: Indents the numbering of the nested entry with the title of\0A  its parent entry. This only has an effect if the entries are numbered\0A  (e.g., via [heading numbering]($heading.numbering)).\0A- [Relative length]($relative): Indents the item by this length\0A  multiplied by its nesting level. Specifying `{2em}`, for instance,\0A  would indent top-level headings (not nested) by `{0em}`, second level\0A  headings by `{2em}` (nested once), third-level headings by `{4em}`\0A  (nested twice) and so on.\0A- [Function]($function): You can completely customize this setting with\0A  a function. That function receives the nesting level as a parameter\0A  (starting at 0 for top-level headings/elements) and can return a\0A  relative length or content making up the indent. For example,\0A  `{n => n * 2em}` would be equivalent to just specifying `{2em}`, while\0A  `{n => [\E2\86\92 ] * n}` would indent with one arrow per nesting level.\0A\0A*Migration hints:*  Specifying `{true}` (equivalent to `{auto}`) or\0A`{false}` (equivalent to `{none}`) for this option is deprecated and\0Awill be removed in a future release.\0A\0A```example\0A#set heading(numbering: \221.a.\22)\0A\0A#outline(\0A  title: [Contents (Automatic)],\0A  indent: auto,\0A)\0A\0A#outline(\0A  title: [Contents (Length)],\0A  indent: 2em,\0A)\0A\0A#outline(\0A  title: [Contents (Function)],\0A  indent: n => [\E2\86\92 ] * n,\0A)\0A\0A= About ACME Corp.\0A== History\0A=== Origins\0A#lorem(10)\0A\0A== Products\0A#lorem(10)\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.730 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [175 x i8] }> <{ [175 x i8] c"Content to fill the space between the title and the page number. Can be\0Aset to `none` to disable filling.\0A\0A```example\0A#outline(fill: line(length: 100%))\0A\0A= A New Beginning\0A```" }>, align 1
