@anon.863986d00e4103fb69f29fe2b65b0919.740 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [614 x i8] }> <{ [614 x i8] c"Represents each entry line in an outline, including the reference to the\0Aoutlined element, its page number, and the filler content between both.\0A\0AThis element is intended for use with show rules to control the appearance\0Aof outlines. To customize an entry's line, you can build it from scratch by\0Aaccessing the `level`, `element`, `body`, `fill` and `page` fields on the\0Aentry.\0A\0A```example\0A#set heading(numbering: \221.\22)\0A\0A#show outline.entry.where(\0A  level: 1\0A): it => {\0A  v(12pt, weak: true)\0A  strong(it)\0A}\0A\0A#outline(indent: auto)\0A\0A= Introduction\0A= Background\0A== History\0A== State of the Art\0A= Analysis\0A== Setup\0A```" }>, align 1
